# FACTS maps a name to {"v": value, "n": item count behind it, "src": where it was measured (a board id, a path in
# this repository, a public URL or a command), "at": when (UTC), "note": caveats}. The page reads every number from
# here at render time, so editing a value here changes the page; no number is typed into the page code. Only v, n,
# src and at are sent to the browser: "note" is for the presenters (it holds the caveats and the earlier readings)
# and never reaches the page. "measured" is the time of the first full reading; a note that starts with FRESH was
# recounted in the "fresh" window and gives the earlier value. None in "v" means not measured or not recorded.
#
# To refresh: run the command or open the file named in "src", edit "v", "n" and "at" here, and restart
# uv run tools/view.py. Numbers from frozen artifacts (studies/*/results) need no refresh; board counts, the event
# log, GPU job records, Exa and past.dev counts move during the event. Never rename a key: tools/demo.py and
# tools/demo_panels.py read them by name.
